  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Your messages queue is cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 7 items are closed (6 at the start plus a pharmacy message that came in while I worked). New lab results arrived midway and changed three of my first decisions, so two refills were cancelled and one was upgraded. Two patients need your review: Price and Odum.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0002). eGFR is 58 (corrected down from 65 today) and an outside HbA1c of 7.1% was drawn 8/19. The patient's request and both pharmacy requests were handled as one, with one order.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg daily: not refilled — needs your review.** I first renewed it, then a corrected creatinine came in today: 1.49 (first reported as 1.36) on the 10/6 BMP. That is a 35% rise over 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase, so it counts the same as potassium ≥5.5. Potassium was 5.2.\n  - I cancelled my refill (mr-t0001) before anything was dispensed.\n  - The original order (mr-00295) now shows stopped and his 30-day supply has run out.\n  - Review task task-t0014 is assigned to you, and the patient got a corrected message.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027)**\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg daily: not refilled — needs your review.** I first renewed it because the 8/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample and didn't count. Then a St. Brigid BMP drawn 10/20 on a good sample arrived today: potassium 5.8.\n  - I cancelled my refill (mr-t0003). The original order (mr-00283) now shows stopped.\n  - Review task task-t0015 is assigned to you, and the patient got a corrected message.\n  - The repeat BMP I ordered (sr-t0004) is probably redundant now. Please keep or cancel it; I told him to wait to hear from you before getting it. His hernia repair is now 11/12.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error (wrong patient's specimen); his valid eGFR is 90–92 and HbA1c is 6.9% (9/28).\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg daily:** renewed for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0013). I first gave a 30-day supply and ordered a BMP, because his last BMP (drawn 10/20/2025) was just over 12 months old. A BMP drawn 10/22 then arrived with potassium 4.6, so I replaced the 30-day order.\n- **Please cancel BMP order sr-t0006** — it's no longer needed and I had no way to cancel lab orders. I told him he doesn't need another blood test for this refill.\n\nEach patient got a reply, and each chart has a signed note: doc-t0019 (Price), doc-t0020 (Odum), doc-t0021 (Webb).\n\n**Still open in your results queue:** the three new results for these patients (inbox-a0001, a0003, a0004). I acted on them but left them for you to sign off. I didn't touch the other results-queue items, which are for other patients. Two of them are critical potassiums: 6.3 for pt-0016 and 6.4 for pt-0008.",
